                                    "text": "param out_gain_db 0 @min -24 @max 12",
                                    "varname": "out_gain_db"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-38",
                                    "linecount": 71,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 577.0, 1043.0 ],
                                    "text": "================================================================================\nclap_cavity_ensemble — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nWHAT IT IS\nA triggered hand clap built like real hands. Each clap is a ~5 ms noise\nburst into the resonance of the air pocket between the palms: cupped hands\nring low and hollow (~500 Hz), flat hands high and sharp (~1.5 kHz). Up to\ntwenty virtual clappers fire together, flammed, or spread over up to a\nsecond. Each one cups a little differently and is re-drawn on every hit from measured\nhand-clap statistics, so no two claps match. A filtered noise tail (a\nshort room, or the long smeared tail of an 808 clap) follows each clap; a\ntight flam shares one tail after its last clap.\n\nEvery hit also drifts the whole group's hand shape slightly (random walk).\nA retrigger while the clap is still sounding flams tighter (the hands are\nalready close) and adds into what is ringing. Nothing resets. With long\nspreads, a new hit reschedules the claps of the previous one that have\nnot landed yet (the new clap restarts the group).\n\nSource: Jylhä & Erkut, DAFx-08 §2-2.1 and Table 1 (ClaPD: per-clap\nresonator f / B / G drawn per hand configuration); Ahmad & Kondoz, DAFx-11\n§5.2, §6.1 (non-repetitive impact sounds).\n\nPARAMETERS (7 + output gain)\n\n1. cavity — 0…100 %, default 50 %\n   Hand shape, following the paper's configurations: cupped A1+ (~500 Hz)\n   -> A1 -> A1- -> A2 -> flat P3 (~1560 Hz). Low = hollow, dubby; high =\n   snappy, cutting.\n\n2. clappers — 1…20 (stepped), default 4\n   People clapping. 1 = a single dry clap; 4-6 = a thick group clap;\n   12-20 = a crowd. Loudness is normalised to how many claps overlap, so\n   it stays about the same (peaks within ~4 dB of the default).\n\n3. spread_ms — 0…1000 ms, default 12 ms\n   How far apart the clappers land (tapered: the first third of the knob\n   covers 0-40 ms). 0 = one fat hit; 10-15 = classic drum-machine flam;\n   30-80 = loose, human group; 300-1000 with many clappers = a burst of\n   applause. Claps more than 30 ms apart each get their own tail; a\n   tighter flam shares one.\n\n4. tail_ms — 20…1500 ms, default 250 ms\n   Noise tail after each clap (time to -40 dB). Short = dry room; long\n   = big trip-hop / space reverb clap.\n\n5. air — 0…100 %, default 50 %\n   Palm-slap brightness on each clap, and how open the tail is. 0 = dark,\n   resonant only; 100 = crisp and splashy.\n\n6. width — 0…100 %, default 60 %\n   Clapper panning and tail decorrelation. 0 = mono.\n\n7. variance — 0…100 %, default 35 %\n   Scales the paper's per-clap deviations and the drift between hits.\n   0 = every clapper exactly on the mean (their timing and personal hand\n   bias still differ).\n\n8. out_gain_db — -24…+12 dB, default 0 dB\n   Final trim, last in the chain.\n\nINLETS / OUTLETS\n- in1: trigger. A single-sample click (any rising edge above 0.1). No\n  velocity: the level is fixed, and variance supplies the movement.\n- out1 / out2: stereo.\n\nNOTES\n- Isolated hits peak around -7…-3 dBFS at defaults. Long tails pile up\n  when rolled fast (+7 dBFS with tail_ms 1500 and air 100).\n- No safety limiter.\n",
                                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                                }
                            }
                        ],
